<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 102,804 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 102,804 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 102,804 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 62,744 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 9,942	    8,603</p>
<p>    Import cargo			92,862	   54,141</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships were expected to sail and nine were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    27,000	 Chilham Castle     due</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    30,000	 Al-Safa	    24/12</p>
<p>High speed deisel    65,000	 Keefan		 due</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Megah    21/12</p>
<p>Crude oil		68,000	 Capitan Mirinda  20/12</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    42,000	 Trade Resolve    25/12</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	    5,350	 Champion Trader  26/12</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Ying Song Hu     26/12</p>
<p>Crude oil		67,600	 Stavros-I	  27/12</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Bunga Selasih    28/12</p>
<p>Tallow		    3,137	 Alam Karang	30/12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
